# Copy to .env.local and restart the studio. Keys stay on the server.

# Enables website ideas, hook generation, and AI drafts. Manual drafts work without it.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional model override (default: gpt-5.6-luna).
# OPENAI_MODEL=

# Maximum OpenAI calls per account per UTC day, including failed attempts (default: 20).
# AI_DAILY_CALL_LIMIT=20

# Local studio only: where the database, images, and renders are stored (default: ./data).
# STUDIO_DATA_DIR=./data

# --- Hosting (Vercel + Supabase) -------------------------------------------
# These three settings turn on accounts and sign-in, and are all a hosted
# studio needs: no database URL, password, or certificate. Setting only some
# of them makes the studio refuse requests until the rest are added.
# All three are in the Supabase dashboard under Project Settings → API Keys.

# Public: browsers use these to sign in.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# Server-only: never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ or share it. The server uses
# it to call Slideo's database functions and to write private storage; signed-
# in browsers get no direct access to either. A legacy service_role key in
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY also works.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...

# Optional: private bucket names (images up to 20 MB; ZIP packages) and the
# largest package in MB (default 50, Supabase's free-plan file limit).
# STORAGE_BUCKET=studio
# STORAGE_EXPORT_BUCKET=studio-exports
# EXPORT_LIMIT_MB=50

# --- TikTok inbox delivery (hosted studios only) ---------------------------
# With all five set, people can connect a TikTok account, and an approved
# slideshow with a planned time can go to their TikTok inbox around then.
# They add a sound and post it in TikTok. Unset, publishing stays manual.

# From your web app in the TikTok developer portal. The secret is server-only:
# never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=
# TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Server-only: 32 random bytes in base64 (openssl rand -base64 32). It
# encrypts stored TikTok tokens and signs links; changing it means every
# connected TikTok account must reconnect.
# TIKTOK_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# The studio's stable public https origin, registered and verified with
# TikTok: the callback is ${APP_URL}/api/tiktok/callback and slide images are
# served under ${APP_URL}/api/tiktok/media/. Deployments on other hosts, such
# as previews, can't use TikTok delivery.
# APP_URL=https://slideo.example.com

# Server-only: the bearer token your scheduler sends to /api/tiktok/tick, at
# least 16 characters. Vercel Cron sends it automatically.
# CRON_SECRET=
